1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:55,111
What he wants! Your fate was sealed the moment you set foot on a ship!

2
00:01:59,111 --> 00:02:01,111
This time, I'll settle things once and for all,

3
00:02:01,111 --> 00:02:03,111
and you'll have no choice but to admit

4
00:02:03,111 --> 00:02:06,111
that the Foxy Pirates are the strongest in the world!

5
00:02:10,111 --> 00:02:14,111
The guy who's closest to invincible and the most dangerous man!

6
00:02:21,111 --> 00:02:23,111
Boss!

7
00:02:23,111 --> 00:02:24,111
Portia!

8
00:02:24,111 --> 00:02:26,111
Panther!

9
00:02:30,111 --> 00:02:32,111
The straw has bit the dust.

10
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:34,111
That was lovely, boss, but what's next?

11
00:02:34,111 --> 00:02:37,111
What do you think? We're going to humiliate them!

12
00:02:37,111 --> 00:02:40,111
The same way they humiliated us in that last Daveyberg fight!

13
00:02:40,111 --> 00:02:43,111
All right, you two, let's begin Operation D!

14
00:02:43,111 --> 00:02:45,111
Yay!

15
00:02:49,111 --> 00:02:52,111
Do you hear that? Sounds like a party.

16
00:02:52,111 --> 00:02:54,111
I wonder what everyone's doing over there.

17
00:02:54,111 --> 00:02:56,111
Why don't you go pay them the visit and find out?

18
00:02:56,111 --> 00:02:58,111
I should be fine watching the ship on my own.

19
00:02:58,111 --> 00:03:00,111
Uh, if something bad happened,

20
00:03:00,111 --> 00:03:02,111
I wouldn't want you to get left here by yourself.

21
00:03:02,111 --> 00:03:04,111
Besides, I'd rather stick around and study.

22
00:03:06,111 --> 00:03:09,111
Why you gotta be so tricky all the time, split-head?

23
00:03:09,111 --> 00:03:12,111
If you want to fight, then come and get it!

24
00:03:12,111 --> 00:03:14,111
Ah!

25
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:16,111
Calm down, Luffy. It'll be okay.

26
00:03:16,111 --> 00:03:17,111
That afro might make you strong,

27
00:03:17,111 --> 00:03:19,111
but right now I think it's making you crazy.

28
00:03:19,111 --> 00:03:21,111
Yep, figures.

29
00:03:21,111 --> 00:03:23,111
All that afro power has gotta go somewhere.

30
00:03:23,111 --> 00:03:25,111
Please tell me that's supposed to be a joke.

31
00:03:25,111 --> 00:03:26,111
Getting revenge is one thing,

32
00:03:26,111 --> 00:03:29,111
but using us to take out his enemies is pretty low.

33
00:03:29,111 --> 00:03:31,111
So what if you had to beat up a couple of losers?

34
00:03:31,111 --> 00:03:33,111
I'm more worried about our goals.

35
00:03:33,111 --> 00:03:35,111
Any way you look at it, he bit off more than he can chew.

36
00:03:35,111 --> 00:03:38,111
He should know better than to get on our bad side.

37
00:03:38,111 --> 00:03:41,111
We'll tear this sorry ship to pieces in no time flat.

38
00:03:41,111 --> 00:03:43,111
You can't beat the five of us.

39
00:03:46,111 --> 00:03:48,111
Or the four of you, at least.

40
00:03:49,111 --> 00:03:51,111
Well, anyway, before we can wreak any havoc,

41
00:03:51,111 --> 00:03:53,111
we have to find a way out of here.

42
00:03:53,111 --> 00:03:54,111
And since this is Foxy's ship,

43
00:03:54,111 --> 00:03:56,111
I'm sure there's some dirty trick involved.

44
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:59,111
I think we can just break through the wall.

45
00:03:59,111 --> 00:04:04,111
What the hell is this place?

46
00:04:04,111 --> 00:04:07,111
Chubby, Chubby, wherever could you be?

47
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:11,111
Are you hiding from me again?

48
00:04:12,111 --> 00:04:16,111
Geez, if you don't come out, I'll have to punish you.

49
00:04:19,111 --> 00:04:20,111
Is something the matter, Doctor?

50
00:04:20,111 --> 00:04:22,111
Uh, no, it's nothing.

51
00:04:23,111 --> 00:04:26,111
Why you, this is the lamest trick you could possibly pull!

52
00:04:26,111 --> 00:04:27,111
Let me handle this!

53
00:04:27,111 --> 00:04:28,111
Luffy!

54
00:04:32,111 --> 00:04:34,111
Listen, I'm on to you!

55
00:04:35,111 --> 00:04:37,111
Tell me where you're hiding, Split Head, now!

56
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:43,111
I don't know what you're talking about!

57
00:04:44,111 --> 00:04:45,111
I wonder where he could be?

58
00:04:45,111 --> 00:04:46,111
Even for Luffy, this is pretty bad.

59
00:04:47,111 --> 00:04:48,111
Should we say something?

60
00:04:48,111 --> 00:04:49,111
This is kind of awkward.

61
00:04:50,111 --> 00:04:51,111
Let's just see how this plays out.

62
00:04:52,111 --> 00:04:53,111
Well, it looks like Split Head's not here, guys!

63
00:04:54,111 --> 00:04:55,111
Behind you!

64
00:04:59,111 --> 00:05:01,111
Luffy, take a closer look at that face.

65
00:05:01,111 --> 00:05:03,111
Okay, but it looks pretty normal to me.

66
00:05:07,111 --> 00:05:08,111
You're not Portia!

67
00:05:08,111 --> 00:05:10,111
You're Split Head's sister, aren't you?

68
00:05:12,111 --> 00:05:13,111
Ah, this is getting me nowhere!

69
00:05:15,111 --> 00:05:16,111
Ah!

70
00:05:16,111 --> 00:05:17,111
It was Split Head all along!

71
00:05:17,111 --> 00:05:19,111
I'm gonna make you pay for tricking me!

72
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:22,111
I don't know if I should laugh or cry about this.

73
00:05:22,111 --> 00:05:24,111
Say a prayer, Strahat!

74
00:05:24,111 --> 00:05:26,111
Slow, slow, boom!

75
00:05:27,111 --> 00:05:28,111
Ah!

76
00:05:30,111 --> 00:05:32,111
Haven't you fools learned your lesson?

77
00:05:32,111 --> 00:05:33,111
Sure you can run,

78
00:05:33,111 --> 00:05:35,111
but my slow, slow beam will always find you!

79
00:05:36,111 --> 00:05:38,111
I've had about enough of that thing.

80
00:05:38,111 --> 00:05:39,111
Yeah, no kidding!

81
00:05:43,111 --> 00:05:44,111
Slow, slow beam!

82
00:05:44,111 --> 00:05:45,111
Ah, look out!

83
00:05:47,111 --> 00:05:48,111
Ah!

84
00:05:48,111 --> 00:05:49,111
Keep your hands off her!

85
00:05:50,111 --> 00:05:51,111
Watch where you're going!

86
00:05:52,111 --> 00:05:53,111
Ah!

87
00:05:53,111 --> 00:05:54,111
Sanjay!

88
00:05:54,111 --> 00:05:55,111
Zoro!

89
00:05:55,111 --> 00:05:56,111
They got hit!

90
00:05:56,111 --> 00:05:58,111
I should have known you dodged, Strahat!

91
00:05:58,111 --> 00:05:59,111
You coward!

92
00:05:59,111 --> 00:06:00,111
Hey!

93
00:06:00,111 --> 00:06:01,111
Stop running away!

94
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:03,111
Come on, just fight us already!

95
00:06:04,111 --> 00:06:05,111
Hey, Nami, let's go!

96
00:06:06,111 --> 00:06:08,111
I'll see you guys when your 30 seconds are up, okay?

97
00:06:09,111 --> 00:06:10,111
No!

98
00:06:10,111 --> 00:06:11,111
Don't leave us like this!

99
00:06:11,111 --> 00:06:12,111
Nami!

100
00:06:12,111 --> 00:06:13,111
Come back!

101
00:06:18,111 --> 00:06:19,111
Wait!

102
00:06:19,111 --> 00:06:20,111
What's that?

103
00:06:20,111 --> 00:06:21,111
There's some kind of note on the door!

104
00:06:22,111 --> 00:06:23,111
Let's see.

105
00:06:23,111 --> 00:06:24,111
Come on!

106
00:06:24,111 --> 00:06:25,111
It's a man's path!

107
00:06:25,111 --> 00:06:26,111
No women allowed!

108
00:06:26,111 --> 00:06:28,111
So, any clue what that's all about?

109
00:06:28,111 --> 00:06:29,111
Nope!

110
00:06:29,111 --> 00:06:30,111
Beats me!

111
00:06:30,111 --> 00:06:31,111
But we better stay on our toes!

112
00:06:31,111 --> 00:06:32,111
No!

113
00:06:32,111 --> 00:06:33,111
No!

114
00:06:36,111 --> 00:06:37,111
Is something the matter, Doctor?

115
00:06:38,111 --> 00:06:39,111
No, it's nothing.

116
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:44,111
That was about to get ugly.

117
00:06:44,111 --> 00:06:46,111
For once, I agree with you.

118
00:06:49,111 --> 00:06:51,111
Looks like a regular old hallway to me.

119
00:06:51,111 --> 00:06:52,111
Yeah.

120
00:06:57,111 --> 00:06:58,111
I take it back!

121
00:06:58,111 --> 00:06:59,111
This is weird!

122
00:07:00,111 --> 00:07:01,111
What kind of place is this?

123
00:07:02,111 --> 00:07:03,111
Oh, I see.

124
00:07:03,111 --> 00:07:04,111
It's like a holding cell under there.

125
00:07:04,111 --> 00:07:08,111
These guys probably did something bad and got locked away as punishment.

126
00:07:09,111 --> 00:07:11,111
They can leer all they want.

127
00:07:11,111 --> 00:07:12,111
I'm going ahead!

128
00:07:12,111 --> 00:07:13,111
Wait!

129
00:07:14,111 --> 00:07:15,111
It's a woman!

130
00:07:15,111 --> 00:07:16,111
All right!

131
00:07:16,111 --> 00:07:17,111
It's been so long!

132
00:07:20,111 --> 00:07:21,111
Ugh!

133
00:07:21,111 --> 00:07:22,111
I can't do it.

134
00:07:22,111 --> 00:07:23,111
I can't give those creeps the satisfaction.

135
00:07:23,111 --> 00:07:24,111
Leave it to me, Nami.

136
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,111
Huh?

137
00:07:26,111 --> 00:07:27,111
What are you...?

138
00:07:27,111 --> 00:07:29,111
Seems like they've been locked up in the dark for a while now.

139
00:07:29,111 --> 00:07:31,111
And if that's the case, they must be weak to light.

140
00:07:32,111 --> 00:07:36,111
All I gotta do is bust out one of my flashballs and they'll be blind as bats in no time.

141
00:07:36,111 --> 00:07:38,111
And then we'll make a break for it, huh?

142
00:07:38,111 --> 00:07:39,111
Right.

143
00:07:39,111 --> 00:07:42,111
Now close your eyes, cause here it comes!

144
00:07:47,111 --> 00:07:48,111
Okay, let's go!

145
00:07:48,111 --> 00:07:49,111
You've got it!

146
00:07:56,111 --> 00:07:57,111
Help me!

147
00:07:57,111 --> 00:07:58,111
I got her!

148
00:07:58,111 --> 00:07:59,111
Musak, no!

149
00:07:59,111 --> 00:08:00,111
My manhood!

150
00:08:00,111 --> 00:08:01,111
Let me touch her too!

151
00:08:01,111 --> 00:08:02,111
Don't worry!

152
00:08:02,111 --> 00:08:04,111
I'll never forget your noble sacrifice!

153
00:08:04,111 --> 00:08:05,111
Don't leave me!

154
00:08:05,111 --> 00:08:07,111
It's been too long!

155
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:08,111
She's so soft!

156
00:08:10,111 --> 00:08:11,111
Is something the matter, Doctor?

157
00:08:12,111 --> 00:08:13,111
No, it's nothing.

158
00:08:16,111 --> 00:08:17,111
That was a close one.

159
00:08:19,111 --> 00:08:20,111
Huh?

160
00:08:20,111 --> 00:08:22,111
Another weird room.

161
00:08:25,111 --> 00:08:26,111
Hey, Nami!

162
00:08:27,111 --> 00:08:28,111
Luffy?

163
00:08:28,111 --> 00:08:29,111
Took you long enough.

164
00:08:29,111 --> 00:08:32,111
What are you doing sitting down in the middle of Foxy's ship?

165
00:08:32,111 --> 00:08:33,111
What am I doing?

166
00:08:33,111 --> 00:08:36,111
I'm eating these rice crackers and having some tea!

167
00:08:36,111 --> 00:08:37,111
Well, duh!

168
00:08:37,111 --> 00:08:38,111
I can tell that much!

169
00:08:38,111 --> 00:08:40,111
You've done well to make it this far!

170
00:08:41,111 --> 00:08:42,111
Congratulations!

171
00:08:42,111 --> 00:08:46,111
But now that you're both here, perhaps I should be congratulating myself instead.

172
00:08:46,111 --> 00:08:50,111
You see, it was my plan to separate you two from the rest of the crew all along!

173
00:08:50,111 --> 00:08:52,111
Luffy I get, but why me?

174
00:08:52,111 --> 00:08:54,111
Because you're obviously the brains of the operation!

175
00:08:54,111 --> 00:08:58,111
With you and the captain out of the picture, the Straw Hats are as good as done for!

176
00:08:58,111 --> 00:09:02,111
I bet those other goons will wipe themselves out long before I get to them!

177
00:09:02,111 --> 00:09:04,111
Hmm, that's a good plan.

178
00:09:05,111 --> 00:09:06,111
This could be bad.

179
00:09:07,111 --> 00:09:09,111
But hey, for now, might as well fight!

180
00:09:09,111 --> 00:09:11,111
Fee-fee-fee-fee!

181
00:09:11,111 --> 00:09:12,111
Right on, brother!

182
00:09:12,111 --> 00:09:13,111
That's what I'd like you to hear!

183
00:09:15,111 --> 00:09:16,111
Oh, yay!

184
00:09:16,111 --> 00:09:19,111
Does this mean we'll finally get our revenge on Straw Hat?

185
00:09:22,111 --> 00:09:24,111
What are those things?

186
00:09:24,111 --> 00:09:25,111
Never seen that one before.

187
00:09:25,111 --> 00:09:27,111
But this one is called Gorilla Pants.

188
00:09:27,111 --> 00:09:28,111
Puncher!

189
00:09:28,111 --> 00:09:30,111
Not pants, it's Gorilla Puncher 13!

190
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,111
Now, get ready!

191
00:09:32,111 --> 00:09:34,111
Here comes the Gorilla Punch!

192
00:09:34,111 --> 00:09:35,111
Leave this one to me, Nami!

193
00:09:35,111 --> 00:09:36,111
Right now!

194
00:09:36,111 --> 00:09:37,111
Gum-gum!

195
00:09:37,111 --> 00:09:39,111
I wouldn't do that if I were you, Rubber Boy!

196
00:09:39,111 --> 00:09:41,111
Remember what happens when you touch the globe?

197
00:09:41,111 --> 00:09:42,111
Stop!

198
00:09:43,111 --> 00:09:44,111
It burns!

199
00:09:46,111 --> 00:09:47,111
You forgot! It is you!

200
00:09:47,111 --> 00:09:48,111
Luffy!

201
00:09:50,111 --> 00:09:52,111
You better not ignore me!

202
00:09:52,111 --> 00:09:56,111
Cause if you do, Mr. Donkey Kicker 18 is gonna stop you, silly!

203
00:09:58,111 --> 00:10:00,111
Hey, Nami!

204
00:10:00,111 --> 00:10:01,111
Huh?

205
00:10:01,111 --> 00:10:03,111
Water, water, water, water, water, water, water, water!

206
00:10:03,111 --> 00:10:04,111
Oh, I see.

207
00:10:04,111 --> 00:10:05,111
That's a good idea!

208
00:10:08,111 --> 00:10:09,111
Wow!

209
00:10:09,111 --> 00:10:10,111
I knew you were pathetic,

210
00:10:10,111 --> 00:10:12,111
but if you think you can beat us with magic tricks,

211
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:13,111
you're just plain crazy!

212
00:10:17,111 --> 00:10:18,111
All right.

213
00:10:18,111 --> 00:10:19,111
Here goes!

214
00:10:23,111 --> 00:10:24,111
Today's forecast is rain!

215
00:10:26,111 --> 00:10:27,111
Thunderstorm?

216
00:10:27,111 --> 00:10:28,111
Tempo!

217
00:10:28,111 --> 00:10:29,111
Nice try!

218
00:10:29,111 --> 00:10:39,111
But it's gonna take more than a little clappy weather to bring down my Gorilla Punch!

219
00:10:39,111 --> 00:10:40,111
Ah!

220
00:10:44,111 --> 00:10:45,111
You really are stupid, aren't you?

221
00:10:45,111 --> 00:10:49,111
If this thing can take punches at lightning, you think a little rain can make any difference?

222
00:10:49,111 --> 00:10:51,111
We won't know until we try, right?

223
00:10:51,111 --> 00:10:53,111
All right, have it your way!

224
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:56,111
Since you clearly don't have any common sense, I'll have to beat some into you!

225
00:10:57,111 --> 00:10:59,111
Gorilla Punch Golden Hips!

226
00:11:00,111 --> 00:11:02,111
Can't burn me now!

227
00:11:06,111 --> 00:11:08,111
Somebody stop him, quick!

228
00:11:08,111 --> 00:11:09,111
Hmm.

229
00:11:09,111 --> 00:11:10,111
Hmm.

230
00:11:10,111 --> 00:11:11,111
Hmm.

231
00:11:11,111 --> 00:11:12,111
Hmm.

232
00:11:12,111 --> 00:11:13,111
Hmm.

233
00:11:13,111 --> 00:11:14,111
Hmm.

234
00:11:14,111 --> 00:11:15,111
Hmm.

235
00:11:15,111 --> 00:11:17,111
Hmm.

236
00:11:17,111 --> 00:11:18,111
Hmm.

237
00:11:18,111 --> 00:11:19,111
Hmm.

238
00:11:19,111 --> 00:11:20,111
Hmm.

239
00:11:27,111 --> 00:11:32,111
...

240
00:11:32,111 --> 00:11:33,111
Aah!

241
00:11:33,111 --> 00:11:36,111
Wh kicked!

242
00:11:36,111 --> 00:11:38,111
Wh kicked!

243
00:11:41,111 --> 00:11:42,111
Ha!

244
00:11:43,111 --> 00:11:44,111
Ha!

245
00:11:44,111 --> 00:11:47,111
Ha-ha. Now come, go!

246
00:11:49,111 --> 00:11:51,111
Ah! Let me go!

247
00:11:56,111 --> 00:11:59,111
Hey, boss, you're not gonna hit us, right?

248
00:12:01,111 --> 00:12:03,111
Holy smoke!

249
00:12:04,111 --> 00:12:05,111
No!

250
00:12:11,111 --> 00:12:13,111
What was that?

251
00:12:14,111 --> 00:12:20,111
Look, it's boss!

252
00:12:20,111 --> 00:12:22,111
Did he beat the Straw Hats?

253
00:12:22,111 --> 00:12:24,111
Men, I've returned!

254
00:12:24,111 --> 00:12:26,111
Yeah!

255
00:12:26,111 --> 00:12:28,111
I got beat!

256
00:12:36,111 --> 00:12:40,111
See? Just like I said, you took too long and they finished the fight without us.

257
00:12:40,111 --> 00:12:43,111
The only reason we're late is because you got lost!

258
00:12:43,111 --> 00:12:49,111
Say, Rubber Boy, I lost fair and square to a fellow pirate so you won't hear me complain. Scan me, turn me in or do whatever you want!

259
00:12:49,111 --> 00:12:54,111
All right, then. In that case, why don't you let them join your crew again?

260
00:12:55,111 --> 00:12:59,111
What? But they stole the Sexy Foxy and stabbed me in the back!

261
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,111
Yeah, so?

262
00:13:01,111 --> 00:13:05,111
I said I wouldn't complain, so have it your way.

263
00:13:05,111 --> 00:13:09,111
All right, men! Straw Hat says you get a free pass, so that's how it's gonna be!

264
00:13:09,111 --> 00:13:11,111
Boss? You mean it?

265
00:13:11,111 --> 00:13:15,111
Go ahead! Talk to them!

266
00:13:15,111 --> 00:13:19,111
Thank you, Straw Hat!

267
00:13:19,111 --> 00:13:25,111
Listen up, frogs! If you wanna be foxes again, then that's fine with me!

268
00:13:25,111 --> 00:13:27,111
Ooh! Ooh!

269
00:13:27,111 --> 00:13:28,111
Yeah!

270
00:13:28,111 --> 00:13:29,111
Well, he's got charisma, if nothing else.

271
00:13:29,111 --> 00:13:31,111
We love you, boss!

272
00:13:31,111 --> 00:13:32,111
Kinda makes me mad!

273
00:13:32,111 --> 00:13:33,111
Boss!

274
00:13:33,111 --> 00:13:35,111
You better not be switching sides on me!

275
00:13:35,111 --> 00:13:50,111
I was just kidding, my darling!

276
00:13:50,111 --> 00:13:51,111
Mother Boy, I just did a head to take care!

277
00:13:51,111 --> 00:13:53,111
You too, Splithead!

278
00:13:56,111 --> 00:13:57,111
So funky!

279
00:13:57,111 --> 00:13:58,111
Yeah!

280
00:13:58,111 --> 00:14:00,111
Oh, no you don't!

281
00:14:00,111 --> 00:14:05,911
Good. I thought you'd never wake up.

282
00:14:05,991 --> 00:14:09,071
Where am I? Last I remember, I was...

283
00:14:09,071 --> 00:14:12,611
Hey! You left me stranded with those creeps!

284
00:14:12,731 --> 00:14:14,951
That's not what happens at all. Did you forget?

285
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:21,731
Oh, when you put it that way, then it all makes sense.

286
00:14:22,011 --> 00:14:25,951
I don't remember beating up all those guys, but I guess I am pretty strong, huh?

287
00:14:30,111 --> 00:14:35,951
Hey, boss, now that we have our old crew back, we're finally done dealing with those horrible straw hat pirates, right?

288
00:14:36,911 --> 00:14:38,111
Not a chance.

289
00:14:38,271 --> 00:14:40,811
Didn't take long for boss to cook up another scheme.

290
00:14:42,191 --> 00:14:45,571
No matter what it takes, we have to cross the straw hats.

291
00:14:45,951 --> 00:14:49,411
Otherwise, we're going to be stuck with this stupid-looking flag for the rest of our lives.

292
00:14:49,931 --> 00:14:52,951
That being said, I think you know our destination.

293
00:14:53,151 --> 00:14:53,511
Yeah!

294
00:14:54,571 --> 00:14:56,331
I'm coming for your upper boy.

295
00:15:00,111 --> 00:15:02,851
Hey, guys! I think I see an island!

296
00:15:03,711 --> 00:15:04,151
Hmm.

297
00:15:05,771 --> 00:15:07,331
Looks uninhabited to me.

298
00:15:07,731 --> 00:15:10,571
Ready, the anchor! Let's go check it out!

299
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,311
Find me some ingredients and I'll start cooking lunch.

300
00:15:13,651 --> 00:15:14,291
All right!

301
00:15:14,851 --> 00:15:16,951
Listen, nothing slimy or gross, okay?

302
00:15:17,351 --> 00:15:20,111
What does it matter? Once it's in your stomach, it's all the same.

303
00:15:20,531 --> 00:15:21,471
Get over yourself.

304
00:15:21,871 --> 00:15:22,091
Ow!

305
00:15:25,691 --> 00:15:26,851
Hey, Sanji!

306
00:15:26,851 --> 00:15:30,431
Hey! We got fish, fruit, and everything! It was easy!

307
00:15:30,571 --> 00:15:31,291
Nice work!

308
00:15:32,331 --> 00:15:32,731
Cheers!

309
00:15:36,071 --> 00:15:36,511
Yummy!

310
00:15:37,191 --> 00:15:39,411
It tastes a lot better if you didn't scarf it down.

311
00:15:39,571 --> 00:15:43,711
I figured you wouldn't have any room left for dinner since you finished off all the snacks on the ship.

312
00:15:43,791 --> 00:15:45,471
I'm just getting warmed up!

313
00:15:45,471 --> 00:15:49,311
That's not good since we've decimated half our supplies already.

314
00:15:49,691 --> 00:15:52,251
Robin, you better eat fast before all the food is gone.

315
00:15:52,471 --> 00:15:54,391
Just let me get to a stopping point first.

316
00:15:54,531 --> 00:15:58,071
Okay, but I heard that if you read too much, you'd turn into a yucky buck.

317
00:15:58,711 --> 00:16:00,311
They call them bookworms.

318
00:16:00,311 --> 00:16:06,991
I found you, Straw Hat.

319
00:16:07,311 --> 00:16:08,911
You kids ready to teach him a lesson?

320
00:16:09,931 --> 00:16:10,891
You bet we are.

321
00:16:10,991 --> 00:16:11,571
Let's go!

322
00:16:11,831 --> 00:16:13,111
Anytime, boss.

323
00:16:13,111 --> 00:16:14,911
One, two, one, two, one.

324
00:16:18,031 --> 00:16:21,131
Hey, boss, they're all looking right this way.

325
00:16:21,311 --> 00:16:22,511
What's the big deal?

326
00:16:22,811 --> 00:16:25,991
Even if they do notice us, they'll think we're just an ordinary crab.

327
00:16:25,991 --> 00:16:27,871
I hope they don't try to eat us.

328
00:16:28,711 --> 00:16:30,371
Is that who I think it is?

329
00:16:30,551 --> 00:16:32,051
Who else would be that stupid?

330
00:16:32,451 --> 00:16:34,351
Don't these guys have anything better to do?

331
00:16:34,531 --> 00:16:36,891
Okay, while they're eating, let's wreck their ship.

332
00:16:38,471 --> 00:16:39,891
What's going on back there?

333
00:16:40,771 --> 00:16:43,011
I caught a crab! Let's eat it!

334
00:16:43,071 --> 00:16:44,511
He's kidding, right?

335
00:16:44,671 --> 00:16:47,631
Nope, and I think he's about to get a nasty surprise.

336
00:16:47,931 --> 00:16:50,071
Stop! We're not food, you fool!

337
00:16:51,771 --> 00:16:54,211
Hey, come back! You look yummy!

338
00:16:54,211 --> 00:16:56,631
Oh, yeah? Then take a bite of this!

339
00:16:58,791 --> 00:17:01,091
Now's our chance! Crab Crab Punch!

340
00:17:02,671 --> 00:17:04,931
The only thing you'll be tasting is the food.

341
00:17:08,711 --> 00:17:12,131
Hey, now! You better learn your place if you know what's good for you, crab.

342
00:17:12,291 --> 00:17:13,311
Now open up!

343
00:17:13,771 --> 00:17:15,231
Because I'm going to eat you!

344
00:17:15,231 --> 00:17:25,431
Wow! I can't believe you guys got eaten by that big crab.

345
00:17:25,591 --> 00:17:26,391
That's pretty lame.

346
00:17:26,571 --> 00:17:28,251
Get that out of your mouth!

347
00:17:28,551 --> 00:17:31,231
Now that that's taken care of, let's get back to our barbecue.

348
00:17:31,771 --> 00:17:33,731
All that crab assing worked out my appetite.

349
00:17:34,151 --> 00:17:35,971
Hey, that isn't done cooking yet.

350
00:17:36,031 --> 00:17:37,771
Whatever. Still tastes good to me.

351
00:17:37,771 --> 00:17:44,931
Come on, boss. I want barbecue, too.

352
00:17:44,991 --> 00:17:45,831
Not too bad!

353
00:17:46,591 --> 00:17:49,011
We didn't come here to eat. We came here to fight.

354
00:17:49,231 --> 00:17:52,931
But don't worry, because soon we'll taste very...

355
00:17:52,931 --> 00:17:55,971
Thank you for waiting, mademoiselle.

356
00:17:56,271 --> 00:17:58,951
I hope that my barbecue special is to your liking.

357
00:17:59,331 --> 00:18:00,691
Oh, you bet!

358
00:18:00,691 --> 00:18:03,231
Here you go. Help yourself.

359
00:18:05,331 --> 00:18:07,811
Oh! This is positively scrumptious!

360
00:18:08,031 --> 00:18:10,431
Why don't you come to Boss's ship and be our cook?

361
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:12,531
Oh, no! Don't tempt me!

362
00:18:12,611 --> 00:18:14,871
If you ask, I might have to say yes!

363
00:18:15,491 --> 00:18:18,191
Please, by all means, don't let me stop you.

364
00:18:19,691 --> 00:18:21,711
Hello? This is the communications room.

365
00:18:23,131 --> 00:18:24,351
Hi, it's me.

366
00:18:24,671 --> 00:18:26,371
Boss has knocked out, so we're done here.

367
00:18:26,551 --> 00:18:27,391
Come and get us, okay?

368
00:18:28,171 --> 00:18:29,931
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm. Don't worry.

369
00:18:30,171 --> 00:18:31,051
Yeah, he'll be fine.

370
00:18:31,531 --> 00:18:33,071
All right, then. See you in a sec.

371
00:18:35,451 --> 00:18:36,951
Bye-bye, Mr. Cook!

372
00:18:37,071 --> 00:18:38,911
I'll never forget your yummy barbecue!

373
00:18:39,311 --> 00:18:40,471
It touched my heart!

374
00:18:40,831 --> 00:18:43,191
Take care, Portia! I'll miss you!

375
00:18:43,771 --> 00:18:45,911
Are you sure you don't want to go back with her?

376
00:18:46,491 --> 00:18:47,251
No way.

377
00:18:47,431 --> 00:18:49,031
You may not appreciate good food,

378
00:18:49,031 --> 00:18:51,511
but Nami and Robin deserve nothing less than the best.

379
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,091
Right, Nami?

380
00:18:54,971 --> 00:18:56,951
Come on, guys! Let's go!

381
00:18:57,251 --> 00:18:59,491
We still need to stock up on some emergency supplies!

382
00:18:59,751 --> 00:19:01,611
Wait for me, Nami-Swan!

383
00:19:08,351 --> 00:19:11,031
Hey, Chopper, did you find any new herbs to use?

384
00:19:11,171 --> 00:19:13,231
Mm-hmm. This place has all sorts of neat stuff.

385
00:19:13,471 --> 00:19:16,311
I got a good stock, but I'm still looking in case I miss something.

386
00:19:16,891 --> 00:19:19,451
Which reminds me, I noticed something weird a second ago.

387
00:19:20,091 --> 00:19:22,111
There's a little groove along the trail here.

388
00:19:22,291 --> 00:19:23,211
I wonder what it is.

389
00:19:23,211 --> 00:19:25,431
Oh, you're right. That is weird.

390
00:19:25,751 --> 00:19:28,511
Looks like a bicycle or something came through here.

391
00:19:28,711 --> 00:19:30,691
Come on, that doesn't make any sense.

392
00:19:30,851 --> 00:19:32,131
There's nobody else on the island.

393
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:33,531
Why would there be a bicycle?

394
00:19:34,191 --> 00:19:35,491
Yeah, that's a good point.

395
00:19:36,791 --> 00:19:37,891
Hey, check it out!

396
00:19:37,951 --> 00:19:39,091
We're almost through the jungle!

397
00:19:42,051 --> 00:19:43,371
Well, that's a letdown.

398
00:19:43,511 --> 00:19:45,411
Just looks like a whole lot of nothing out here.

399
00:19:45,411 --> 00:19:49,831
He's excited. Did I miss something?

400
00:19:50,211 --> 00:19:51,291
I don't get it either.

401
00:19:51,651 --> 00:19:53,371
Maybe he found some new herbs.

402
00:19:54,291 --> 00:19:54,751
Huh?

403
00:19:56,491 --> 00:19:57,511
Chopper, you cheater!

404
00:19:57,671 --> 00:20:00,351
You were going to hog that big mushroom all to yourself, weren't you?

405
00:20:00,471 --> 00:20:01,371
Get back here!

406
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:05,551
Hey! What happened? Are you okay?

407
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:07,491
There must be something behind that rock.

408
00:20:07,651 --> 00:20:08,231
Come on, hurry!

409
00:20:08,231 --> 00:20:12,711
Whoa! You're not a mushroom!

410
00:20:18,131 --> 00:20:20,891
Hmm? A raccoon dog.

411
00:20:21,131 --> 00:20:23,131
Can't you see the antlers? I'm a reindeer!

412
00:20:23,711 --> 00:20:25,571
I saw you fall! Are you hurt?

413
00:20:26,331 --> 00:20:27,771
Who the heck is that?

414
00:20:29,351 --> 00:20:30,311
What's going on?

415
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,231
I don't know. Someone's here.

416
00:20:32,651 --> 00:20:34,611
Do you mind? I was sleeping.

417
00:20:34,871 --> 00:20:36,071
Did you hit my friend?

418
00:20:36,071 --> 00:20:39,151
Oh, man! That guy is huge!

419
00:20:39,211 --> 00:20:40,831
I thought we were alone on this island!

420
00:20:44,811 --> 00:20:50,031
You know him?

421
00:20:51,991 --> 00:20:53,511
Hey, is this guy an enemy?

422
00:20:53,811 --> 00:20:54,671
Who is he?

423
00:20:55,631 --> 00:20:58,011
If Robin's freaking out, then so am I!

424
00:20:58,531 --> 00:20:59,351
Something's wrong.

425
00:21:00,371 --> 00:21:01,731
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Hold on.

426
00:21:01,851 --> 00:21:05,131
Look, I know you're surprised to see me, but don't get so worked up.

427
00:21:05,131 --> 00:21:07,891
It's not like I came here on official orders or anything.

428
00:21:08,071 --> 00:21:10,951
It's a nice day, so I decided to go for a ride.

429
00:21:11,151 --> 00:21:13,451
Orders, huh? And who is it you work for?

430
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:15,111
He's a marine.

431
00:21:15,491 --> 00:21:19,091
Not only that, he's known as one of the world government's ultimate powerhouses.

432
00:21:20,391 --> 00:21:21,391
What, for real?

433
00:21:21,771 --> 00:21:22,891
I'm afraid so.

434
00:21:23,591 --> 00:21:26,271
This is Admiral Aokiji from Navy Headquarters.

435
00:21:26,271 --> 00:21:31,171
My, my, you've grown into quite the lovely lady, haven't you?

436
00:21:31,811 --> 00:21:32,851
Nico Robin?

437
00:21:32,851 --> 00:21:45,551
My, my, my

438
00:21:45,551 --> 00:21:45,891
Yes!

439
00:21:45,891 --> 00:21:46,391
It's a real one for us.

440
00:21:46,391 --> 00:21:55,291
To be gone

441
00:23:06,084 --> 00:23:09,924
Next, One Piece, Navy Headquarters Admiral Aokiji,

442
00:23:09,924 --> 00:23:12,584
the ferocity of an ultimate powerhouse.

443
00:23:12,584 --> 00:23:14,724
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

